1: /**
2:  * Shared plan-critic approval recording (issues #2012, #2002 async parity).
3:  *
4:  * ONE approval implementation serves BOTH Task transports:
5:  *
6:  *  - the synchronous `tool.execute.after` path in the delegation gate (the
7:  *    critic child returned inline), and
8:  *  - the native async completion path (OpenCode 2.3 background subagents),
9:  *    where the trusted terminal result is delivered later through the
10:  *    background completion observer.
11:  *
12:  * Both callers must establish, BEFORE calling
13:  * {@link recordVerifiedPlanCriticApproval}, that the verdict text comes from a
14:  * host-verified critic child whose durable dispatch identity (parent session,
15:  * call id, role) is known. This module never trusts ambient session state —
16:  * every identity field is passed explicitly and embedded in the approval
17:  * audit metadata.
18:  *
19:  * Safety contract (fail-closed):
20:  *  - Only an `APPROVED` verdict ({@link extractPlanCriticVerdict}) records a
21:  *    snapshot. `NEEDS_REVISION`, `REJECTED`, missing, or unparseable verdicts
22:  *    never approve anything.
23:  *  - When the caller supplies `dispatchPlanStructureHash` (the async
24:  *    transport, captured at dispatch time and persisted on the delegation
25:  *    record), the CURRENT plan's structural hash must still equal it. A plan
26:  *    edited after the critic was dispatched cannot be approved by the old
27:  *    verdict — the caller is told to re-run the critic instead.
28:  *  - Replay safety: before writing, the ledger is scanned for an existing
29:  *    `plan_critic_gate` approval snapshot bound to the same `call_id`. A
30:  *    replay of the same terminal (crash recovery, duplicate completion event)
31:  *    is a no-op, so a terminal can never approve twice.
32:  *  - The snapshot itself is written through the single existing choke point
33:  *    `takeSnapshotEvent` (`source: 'critic_approved'`, structural-hash
34:  *    payload) — the exact shape `assertPlanCriticApprovedForExecution` and
35:  *    `loadLastPlanCriticApprovedSnapshot` already verify. No competing
36:  *    approval implementation exists.
37:  */
38: 
39: import type { Plan } from '../config/plan-schema';
40: import { log, warn } from '../utils/logger';
41: import {
42: 	computePlanStructureHash,
43: 	readLedgerEventsWithIntegrity,
44: 	takeSnapshotEvent,
45: } from './ledger';
46: import { loadPlanJsonOnly } from './manager';
47: import { derivePlanId } from './utils';
